    "diag": [
     "Measles: **IgM serology** and **PCR** (throat/nasopharyngeal swab, urine); notifiable – call ahead, do not let a suspected case sit in a waiting room.",
     "Mumps: PCR from saliva/buccal swab, IgM.",
     "Rubella in pregnancy: IgM, IgG, avidity; **immune status = rubella IgG (antibody detection)** – e.g. a woman unsure if vaccinated.",
     "Proof of measles immunity: measles IgG or documented 2 doses of MMR."
    ],
    "beh": [
     "No specific antiviral; supportive. **Vitamin A** reduces measles mortality in malnourished children (WHO).",
     "Measles post-exposure: MMR within 72 h or **immunoglobulin within 6 days** for susceptible infants, pregnant women and immunocompromised (passive immunisation)."
    ],
    "hand": [
     "**MMR = live attenuated triple vaccine**, one serotype each → excellent, long-lasting protection (≥95% after 2 doses).",
     "Sweden: general MMR for boys and girls **since 1982**; today **18 months and 6–8 years** (the original 1982 schedule was 18 months and 10–12 years).",
     "**Contraindicated in pregnancy and severe immunosuppression** (live vaccine); avoid pregnancy ~1 month after vaccination; susceptible women vaccinated after delivery.",
     "Autism link with MMR has been **disproved**.",
     "Measles requires **airborne precautions**; staff without immunity must not care for cases."
    ],
    "flagg": [
     "Infection requiring **~95% herd immunity = measles** (R0 12–18).",
     "**Koplik spots** + fever, cough, conjunctivitis → rash = measles; late complication **SSPE**.",
     "Rubella immune status = **antibody (IgG) detection**.",
     "MMR is **live** → not in pregnancy or severe immunodeficiency.",
     "Mumps: parotitis, meningitis, orchitis (fertility), deafness.",
     "Measles causes **immune amnesia** – loss of pre-existing immune memory."
    ],
